WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.067
So what impact

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.501
will this

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.236
have actually on the battlefield?

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:03.636
Well, let's start

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.804
with the tanks themselves.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.472
This is the German

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.507
Shepherd, very similar to the Abrams.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.341
Highly capable,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.175
certainly more capable

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.011
than the Russian made T-72,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.679
which the Ukrainians have tended

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.681
to rely on. But here's a key point.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.483
Also, an offensive weapon

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.317
with Ukrainians,

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.752
as you heard from the defense minister.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.519
They're hoping that

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.122
this will help them retake territory

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.556
that Russia has occupied

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.691
since the start of this invasion.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.159
So let's look at the numbers, though.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.395
Here are the tanks by country so far,

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:30.563
any disunity clearly has dissolved.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.331
You've got America.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:31.898
You're Germany,

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.901
the U.K., also Poland, sending tanks in.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.136
But look at these numbers here.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.637
That total from these

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.407
three countries is 59 tanks with others,

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.242
you get closer to 100.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.176
How does that fit into

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.944
the broader picture in Ukraine?

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.980
We don't know how many tanks exactly

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.648
Russia and Ukraine are using.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.283
We just don't trust their numbers.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.017
We do know

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:51.951
or have a good sense

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:52.886
of how many been lost

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:53.787
since the start of the war.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.721
These are numbers

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.789
compiled by Oryx,

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.357
and they based this on open source,

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.159
but only what they can confirm

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.194
via video seeing tanks destroyed.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.328
And so far,

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.431
more than 600 Russian tanks,

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.266
close to 500 Ukrainian tanks.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.968
That's more than 2000 tanks lost.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.003
Gives you a sense

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.672
of how many are on the battlefield there.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.907
And then you compare

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:14.674
that 59,

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.743
perhaps it gets up to 100 over the next

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.744
several months.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.812
Even the president

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.512
granted there

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.246
it's going to take time

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.414
to get them in there.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.916
The math doesn't add up in terms

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.850
of leveling

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.218
the playing field between what

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.153
Russia has, what Ukraine has.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.021
And here's one more point

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.222
I would make when I speak to U.S.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.090
military officials.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.859
There is a school of thought among U.S.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.693
officials

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.828
that Ukraine

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:35.728
is not

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.231
ideally equipped for a big tank battle.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.332
It's much better

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.734
equipped for smaller, more mobile units.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.303
That's where they had all the success

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.270
destroying Russian

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.572
tanks in the early stages

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.407
of the war around Kiev.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.142
That's why this weapon system

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.843
with which the U.S.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.543
has also sent

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.144
in the Bradley

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.178
Fighting Vehicle,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.780
which, by the way, has anti-tank

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.281
capabilities with the TOW missile

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.316
mounted here

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.218
just on the left side of its turret

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.152
there are many in the U.S.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:01:59.853
that believe

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.554
that's the better path for Ukraine.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.322
Smaller,

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.857
lighter, more mobile,

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.525
requiring less support

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.227
than trying to beat the Russians.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.429
A tank warfare in the East

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:11.731
Those

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.233
TOW anti-tank missiles

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.801
are really, really important.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.902
Jim Sciutto, stay with us.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.137
I want to get some analysis

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.037
right now as well

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.572
from CNN's Kate Bolduan.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.440
And retired U.S.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.841
Army General Wesley Clark.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.743
He's a CNN military analyst.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:26.012
General Clark, how critical is this move?

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.381
Alisyn, both Leppard and Abrams

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.183
battle tanks to Ukraine.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:30.984
And is the U.S.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.552
doing everything possible

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.621
to address the potential complications

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.257
associated with the Abrams tanks?

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.461
Well, I think all these tanks

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.762
being provided is really,

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.197
really essential

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:47.333
because even as late as last summer,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.668
six months ago,

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.370
Ukrainians were running out

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.804
of main gun ammunition

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.806
for their T-72 tanks.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.875
And there's a worldwide shortage,

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.111
just 125 millimeter ammunition.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.445
So they needed

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.947
and they've been asking for our tanks

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.282
for months with tanks.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.416
Still aren't there, of course.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.251
And as Jim Sciutto pointed out,

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:05.952
they're going

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:06.786
what's going to be

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.655
there is a small number compared to what

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.789
their need is.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.991
So, yes, the tanks are important.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.059
They're more important

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.761
as a symbol of U.S.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.863
and European commitment.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.965
But in the defense,

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.967
you've got to have some armor

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.835
for local reserves.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.703
So we are here to

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.004
talk about the iron fist

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.172
and taking back the territory.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.140
That's good.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.441
What we're also

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:29.576
facing the prospect

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.778
of a major Russian offensive.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.780
And if that Russian offensive comes,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.581
the tanks,

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.349
even these small numbers of tank

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.318
could be very significant.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.286
If they get to the right spot

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.155
to cut off the penetration,

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.389
you know, that's a good point.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:43.556
You know,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:43.990
Katie Bowe,

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.958
you're doing a lot of reporting

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:45.992
on this as well.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:46.526
What are you hearing?

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.393
What does this U.S.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.127
decision say

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.763
about their view of the timeline

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.098
of how long this war

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.033
could actually drag on?

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.501
Wolf, what I think is really telling

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.136
is the way that Biden administration

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.538
officials are framing the decision

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.505
to send the Abrams.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.306
They're framing it

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.674
as a long term commitment

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.109
to Ukraine's capabilities,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.344
which really backs up

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.446
what I think we've been hearing from U.S.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.814
intelligence and military officials

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.514
for a while now,

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.749
which is that they don't see this war

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.050
winding down anytime soon.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.619
Ukraine obviously

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.520
is not planning on stopping fighting.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.388
And I spoke to a senior

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.123
Western intelligence official last week

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:17.790
who said, look,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.392
all the indications that we have is

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.094
that Putin is convinced,

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.228
that is still convinced

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.396
that he can defeat

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.931
Ukraine militarily on the battlefield.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.132
So at this point, U.S.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.066
officials don't believe

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.835
that there is a negotiated settlement

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.370
in the cards any time soon.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.437
They also don't believe that

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.405
there is a decisive

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.240
military resolution coming

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:34.941
anytime soon,

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:35.975
which is exactly what you heard

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.377
from chairman of the Joint Chiefs

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.711
General Mark Milley last week,

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.812
telling reporters

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.380
that he believed

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.547
it would be incredibly difficult

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.750
for Ukraine to eject Russia

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.051
from all of its territory

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:45.885
within the next year.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:46.252
So, Wolf,

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.054
that's the context in which U.S.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.589
officials are making this decision

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.191
on the Abrams a long, hard slog.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.061
Jim, in that context, what specifically

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.330
will Ukraine try to accomplish

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.631
in the short run,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.732
in the short term,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.167
in the coming months, let's say,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.268
with the German

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.603
Shepherd battle tanks

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.904
and eventually the U.S.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.272
Abrams tanks arriving,

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.041
their hope is to take back territory.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.275
That's their intention.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:09.942
They don't want to rest

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.144
on their laurels, laurels.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.112
They don't want to sue for peace

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.180
and grant territory

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.114
in exchange for peace.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:15.548
You heard from

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:16.482
the defense minister there.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.885
He hopes that these tanks will be part

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:21.020
of an offensive that can punch through

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.388
Russian lines, in effect.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.856
And we should not

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.793
diminish Ukraine's ability to do

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.660
counter offensives.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.162
They had enormous success

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.230
just a few months ago around hockey.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.699
Surprising everybody really

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.767
with the speed of their advance there.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:35.668
But the fact is,

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:36.669
the battlefield in the east

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.303
is different now.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.971
It's more dug in its flatlands.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:39.672
There are trenches.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.274
There are artillery pieces.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.743
There are tank divisions there.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.477
And that's one reason

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.312
we've seen the casualty count,

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.413
the daily casualty count.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.349
They're so horrific.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.651
So those are Ukrainian hopes.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:52.218
They hope that

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.786
this will make a different difference.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.188
But as Katie Bowe said

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.756
from the U.S., perspective,

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.623
they don't expect this

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.659
to be winding down anytime soon.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:05:59.959
The U.S.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:02.261
expects us to be a grinding

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.997
continuation of months and months of war.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.200
Yeah, that's that's what they expect.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.202
General Clark, what does this say

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:10.370
that the Western allies

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.238
finally took this step today,

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.073
despite all of Russia's

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:17.910
very public and private threats

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.246
John, you know, this is

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.180
the policy

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.348
is to slowly

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.384
ramp up the assistance to Ukraine.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.319
And at every step,

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.621
yes, Moscow is going to object,

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:29.689
but not to do it

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.591
in such an abrupt way

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.659
that it triggers an escalation,

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.796
a real escalation to nuclear joke.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.098
This is the administration's strategy

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.533
to keep the war going,

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.567
lead Russia,

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.969
support Ukraine, hope

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:46.305
that Ukraine can win, but don't do enough

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:49.976
to totally turn it upside down suddenly

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.611
so Putin can knee

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:54.013
jerk wise use nuclear weapons.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.348
And that's that's

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:57.116
the goal of the administration.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.185
This is perfectly and part of it.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.486
Dramatic developments, indeed.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:01.988
Guys, thank you very, very much.

